      "message": "init: reject -port=65535 when the onion port has to be derived from it\n\nThe default onion bind uses -port + 1. For -port=65535 that wraps to 0,\nso the node binds 127.0.0.1 to a random port and points the automatic\nTor onion service at it.\n\nReturn an init error instead when that port is actually needed (no\nexplicit onion bind port and listening is enabled). An explicit\n-bind=<addr>:<port>=onion keeps working.",
